Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||01-09-2001||12:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B><P>I know there was an article on the net somewhere about adding a Formula/GT rear swaybar on a coupe, but I can't remember where.  Try the Online Service Guide, I think it was there.<P>anywho, good luck<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>If you have all the parts (bar, brackets that bolt up to the struts, saddle bushings and endlinks) it should be the same as adding it to a GT/Formula. The holes are drilled and everything. <BR>||||reg||1
